#base main
#opened 2026-11-09
#head 9ec09215aa345fa6826fe150fb0b35f7e2e7d8a8
#describe what CI gets an e2e job (four headless Playwright/Electron suites under xvfb) and a coverage job (job summary plus uploaded coverage artifact), with no external service or secret. README and CONTRIBUTING now say so.
#describe before CI ran typecheck, lint and the unit tests, and built; e2e and coverage never ran there.
#describe after Integrations, tray, pull request host and skills e2e run on the runner; the graph suite does not, because WebGL is unavailable under xvfb. A coverage table is written to the job summary; either failing turns CI red.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint, the CI workflow test and a full coverage run are green, and the e2e job passed on the runner.
~ .github/workflows/ci.yml
~ CONTRIBUTING.md
~ README.md
~ test/ci-workflow.test.ts
#order .github/workflows/ci.yml
#order test/ci-workflow.test.ts
#order README.md
#order CONTRIBUTING.md
#reason .github/workflows/ci.yml LAN-115: CI never ran the e2e suites or showed coverage, so regressions there went unseen until a local run.
#reason CONTRIBUTING.md It described CI as three commands with no Electron, and named a guard test that no longer checks that.
#reason README.md It said CI never runs Electron or the Playwright e2e, which stopped being true with the e2e and coverage jobs.
#reason test/ci-workflow.test.ts The old guards forbade any upload or Electron step, so they had to say where the new ones are allowed without going soft.
#story A pull request now shows e2e and coverage results
#step actor A contributor
#step action opens a pull request
#step subject the repository's CI
#file .github/workflows/ci.yml
#below interaction Sees e2e results and a coverage table in the run
#below consequence e2e and coverage only ran on a developer's machine => CI runs both and fails when either fails
#story The workflow guard stays strict
#step actor A maintainer
#step action edits the CI workflow
#step subject its text guard
#file test/ci-workflow.test.ts
#below interaction Is told when a step breaks the CI rules
#below consequence any upload or Electron step was refused => only the e2e and coverage jobs may have them
